.TH ZERODDS-COAP-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-coap-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-coap-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/coap-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the CoAP bridge daemon maps DDS topics onto CoAP
resources. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-coap-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the parser that reads it is
.IR crates/coap-bridge/src/daemon/config.rs::load_from_str .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " coap ", " proxy ", " oscore ", " auth ", " acl ", " metrics ", " content_format ", " topics ", " tenants .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr and starts with the
defaults \(em watch the WARN log.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
The threshold of the daemon's log: one JSON object per line on stdout with
.IR timestamp ", " level ", " event
and the fields of the event (spec \(sc8.1). Each exchange is an event
.IR request ,
at
.I debug
for a 2.xx response,
.I info
for 4.xx,
.I warn
for 5.xx.
.SS coap
.TP
.B bind
UDP listen address for
.IR coap:// ,
e.g.
.IR "0.0.0.0:5683" .
.TP
.B bind_dtls
Separate listen address for
.IR coaps:// .
Without it the daemon uses
.B bind
with the port raised by one.
.TP
.B max_message_size
DoS cap per datagram in bytes. Default
.I 1152
per RFC 7252; raise it only behind a jumbo MTU. A larger datagram is
.I 4.13
with Size1.
.TP
.B max_body_size
The largest body a Block1 transfer assembles, in bytes. Default
.IR 65536 ;
beyond it
.I 4.13
with Size1 (RFC 7959 \(sc2.9.3).
.TP
.B block_size
16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512 or 1024. A representation larger than it goes
out in Block2 blocks of this size (RFC 7959). Default
.IR 1024 .
.TP
.B ack_timeout_ms
CON retransmission timeout in milliseconds, of the Confirmable
notifications and pings too (RFC 7252 \(sc4.2).
.TP
.B max_retransmit
Number of CON retransmissions before the exchange is given up; an
observer that does not acknowledge a Confirmable notification after them
is removed (RFC 7641 \(sc4.5).
.TP
.B observe_max_age_secs
The longest an observer goes without acknowledging a notification: after
it the next notification is Confirmable, also on a BEST_EFFORT topic (RFC
7641 \(sc4.5 sets 24 hours as the bound;
.I 0
leaves that bound). Default
.IR 60 .
.TP
.B keep_alive_secs
The period of the daemon's CoAP ping (an empty Confirmable message) to
each endpoint with an observation; an endpoint that answers neither with
Reset nor with ACK after the retransmissions loses its observations
(spec \(sc6, Liveliness).
.I 0
sends none, the default.
.TP
.B multicast
Sub-map for requests to IP multicast groups (RFC 7252 \(sc8):
.B enabled
(boolean, default false),
.B groups
(the groups joined; default the all-CoAP-nodes group of the bind
address's family, 224.0.1.187 or ff02::fd and ff05::fd),
.B interface_v4
and
.B interface_v6
(interface address and interface index a group is joined on),
.B leisure_ms
(the period a response is sent in, default 5000),
.B resources
(the resources that answer a multicast request, default
.IR .well-known/core )
and
.B unauthenticated_resources
(those that answer one without OSCORE, default
.IR .well-known/core ).
.TP
.B dtls
Sub-map with
.B enabled
(boolean),
.B ca_file
(trust anchor),
.BR cert_file " and " key_file
(server material),
.B cipher_suites
(list of IANA names \(em an unknown name aborts the start instead of being
dropped) and
.B psk
(list of pre-shared keys, each entry carrying
.BR identity " and " secret_hex ),
.B rpk_key_file
(the PEM private key whose public key the daemon shows as its raw public
key, RFC 7250) and
.B rpk_trusted
(the RFC 6920 names of the client keys it accepts:
.IR ni: ,
.I nih:
or the hex of the binary form, at least
.IR sha-256-120 ).
.SS proxy
The daemon as a CoAP-to-CoAP proxy (RFC 7252 \(sc5.7; specification \(sc4.7).
.TP
.B forward
Boolean, default false. Carry out requests with
.B Proxy-Uri
or
.BR Proxy-Scheme ;
without it such a request is
.I 5.05
unless it names the daemon itself.
.TP
.B schemes
List, default
.IR "[coap, coaps]" .
.TP
.B names
Host names that name this daemon (a request for one of them is local);
the first is the identifier of a
.I 5.08
diagnostic.
.TP
.B timeout_ms
Default 10000; then
.BR "5.04 Gateway Timeout" .
.TP
.B reverse
List of
.BR path " and " origin :
the resources under
.B path
are those under the
.B origin
URI. A path that covers a topic or
.I .well-known/core
stops the start.
.TP
.B cache_entries
Default 256.
.TP
.B require_dtls_for_coaps
Boolean, default true: a request for a
.I coaps
destination must come over DTLS.
.TP
.B max_hops
Initial Hop-Limit (RFC 8768), default 16.
.TP
.B multicast_wait_ms
How long a request to a multicast destination collects responses,
default 5000.
.TP
.B dtls
Sub-map for
.I coaps
destinations:
.B ca_file
(trust anchors the destination's certificate is checked against),
.BR cert_file " and " key_file
(the certificate the proxy presents),
.BR psk_identity " and " psk_secret_hex ,
or
.B rpk_key_file
and
.B rpk_trusted
(its raw public key and the RFC 6920 names of the destinations' keys).
.SS oscore
Object Security for Constrained RESTful Environments, RFC 8613 \(em end-to-end
protection that survives a CoAP proxy (\(sc7.2).
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. With
.IR true ,
.B master_secret_hex
is mandatory; the daemon refuses to start without it.
.TP
.B master_secret_hex
OSCORE master secret, hex.
.TP
.B master_salt_hex
OSCORE master salt, hex.
.TP
.B id_context_hex
OSCORE ID context, hex.
.TP
.B sender_id_hex
Sender ID of this daemon. Default
.IR 01 .
.TP
.B replay_window
Width of the anti-replay window.
.SS auth
.TP
.B mode
.IR none " | " bearer " | " jwt " | " mtls .
A ZeroDDS extension; the CoAP bridge spec secures with DTLS and OSCORE only.
.I bearer
and
.I jwt
read the token from CoAP option 65000
.RI ( "Bearer <token>" ).
.I mtls
takes the identity of the DTLS handshake and needs
.BR coap.dtls.enabled :
the client certificate's subject DN (RFC 4514; an ACL entry may name its
fingerprint
.I mtls:<SHA-256 hex>
instead) or
.IR psk:<PSK identity> .
.TP
.B bearer_token
Shared token accepted when
.B mode
is
.IR bearer .
.TP
.B bearer_subject
Subject that single token authenticates as.
.TP
.B jwt
Sub-map for
.BR jwt :
.B public_key
(PEM file: an RSA key, PKCS#1 or SubjectPublicKeyInfo, for RS256; a P-256
SubjectPublicKeyInfo for ES256; the token's
.I alg
has to be the key's algorithm),
.BR issuer ,
.BR audience ,
.B required_claim
.RI ( claim=value ;
a space-separated claim such as
.I scope
matches when it contains the value).
.I exp
and
.I nbf
are enforced with 60 s leeway. The subject is the
.I sub
claim. Without
.B public_key
the daemon does not start (exit 1).
.SS acl
Daemon-side access control per CoAP resource path. The subject is the one
.B auth.mode
yields:
.I anonymous
for
.IR none ,
the token's subject for
.IR bearer " and " jwt ,
the DTLS identity for
.IR mtls .
.TP
.B default_deny
Boolean.
.I true
denies a resource no rule names, also without any rule;
.I false
opens the unnamed rest. Not set: a resource no rule names is denied once a
rule exists or an auth mode other than
.I none
is set; with neither, every resource is open.
.TP
.B rules
List of subject-keyed rules. Each entry carries
.B subject
plus the resource-path lists
.B allow_post
(write) and
.B allow_observe
(read).
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9093"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision.
The key is
.BR listen ,
not
.IR address .
.TP
.B path
The path of the Prometheus page. Default
.IR /metrics .
.SS content_format
The Content-Format number of each form of a sample (spec \(sc4.5); no two
forms may share one.
.TP
.B cdr2_le_id
XCDR2 little endian, default
.IR 65000 .
.TP
.B cdr2_be_id
XCDR2 big endian, default
.IR 65001 .
.TP
.B cdr1_le_id
XCDR1 little endian, default
.IR 65002 .
.TP
.B json_id
JSON, default
.IR 50 .
.TP
.B cbor_id
CBOR, default
.IR 60 .
.SS topics (list)
.TP
.B dds_name
DDS topic name.
.TP
.B dds_type
Fully-qualified IDL type.
.TP
.B coap_uri_path
CoAP resource path. Defaults to a slug of
.BR dds_name .
.TP
.B direction
.IR in " | " out " | " bidir .
.I in
carries CoAP POST/PUT requests into DDS (the daemon creates a DataWriter),
.I out
carries DDS samples to CoAP clients through GET and Observe (a DataReader),
.I bidir
both. Default
.IR bidir .
.TP
.B idl_file
The IDL file that declares
.B dds_type
(its
.I #include
files are read from its directory). With it the topic takes and gives
JSON, CBOR, XCDR1 and both XCDR2 byte orders, a body is checked against
the type, DELETE takes a sample, and
.I GET /schema/<slug>
returns the IDL. A file that does not load stops the start.
.TP
.B extensibility
.IR final " | " appendable " | " mutable :
the XCDR2 header of a topic without
.BR idl_file ,
whose samples pass through. Default
.I appendable
(DDS-XTypes 1.3 \(sc7.3.1.2.1.8).
.TP
.B data_representation
.IR xcdr2 " | " xcdr1 :
what the topic's DDS writer offers and sends. Default
.IR xcdr2 ;
.I xcdr1
needs
.B idl_file
and serves DDS readers that accept only XCDR1.
.TP
.B qos
DDS QoS sub-map:
.B reliability
.RI ( reliable :
Confirmable notifications;
.IR best_effort ),
.B durability
.RI ( volatile :
a new observer gets no sample;
.IR transient_local ", " transient ", " persistent :
the last ones),
.B history
with
.B kind
.RI ( keep_last " | " keep_all )
and
.B depth
(how many of the last samples a new observer gets),
.B lifespan_ms
(the Max-Age of a sample),
.B deadline_ms
(after this without a sample a GET is
.I 5.03
with Max-Age 0 and every observation ends with one),
.B liveliness_lease_ms
and
.B partition
(a list; both go to the topic's DDS endpoints).
.SS tenants (list)
Participants beside the one of
.B domain
(spec \(sc1 L6). A DTLS session whose subject a tenant names is bound to
it: its requests address the tenant's topics only. Plaintext requests and
the sessions no tenant names address the top-level
.BR topics .
.TP
.B name
Unique; the
.I topic
label of the tenant's metrics is
.IR <name>/<dds_name> .
.TP
.B domain
The DDS domain of the tenant's participant. Default: the top-level
.BR domain .
.TP
.B subjects
The DTLS subjects bound to the tenant:
.IR psk:<identity> ,
the certificate's subject DN or
.IR mtls:<sha256> ,
.IR rpk:<ni URI> .
A subject is bound to one tenant at most.
.TP
.B topics
As the top-level
.BR topics .
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/coap-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-coap-bridged (1).
